 * `conc.group` and `time.group` to indicate the concentrations and times that
   have not been filtered for the interval.
 
+Values given per observation (the urine volume and collection duration,
+`include_half.life`, `exclude_half.life`, and a per-observation `lloq`) follow
+their observation through imputation, and an observation is identified by its
+time.  So a function that adds or drops observations must keep the times of the
+others, and a function that changes times must keep the number of observations
+and their order (the values then stay in order).  A function that both adds and
+drops observations in one step cannot be told apart from one that moved an
+observation, so the observation at the new time is treated as added, with a
+warning (`pknca_warning_impute_obs_values_dropped`) when a value of a dropped
+observation is lost; split such a function into two imputation methods instead.
+An observation the function adds has a collection volume of 0, no collection
+duration, is neither included in nor excluded from the half-life, and has the
+profile's `lloq` when that is constant (and a missing `lloq` when it varies).
+
